<%
  scene = roll.scene
  game = scene.game_session
  character = roll.player.character
  hero = roll.player.name
  modifier, statuses, margin = [ roll.modifier, roll.status_modifier, roll.margin ].map { format("%+d", it) }
  used = character.items.used_since(scene.created_at).map do |item|
    "#{item.name} (#{format("%+d", item.hp_effect)} health)"
  end
  attempts = game.party.reject(&:departed?).map do |player|
    "#{player.name} tried #{player.attempts.to_sentence.presence || "nothing"}"
  end
  parts = game.party.many? ? ", each with a part in it" : ""
  witness = game.party.one? ? "the hero sees and hears" : "the heroes see and hear"
%>
Scene <%= scene.position %> of <%= game.scene_budget %>, <%= scene.part_of_the_story %>.
<%= hero %> chose "<%= roll.choice.label %>".
Die <%= roll.value %>, modifier <%= modifier %>, statuses <%= statuses %>.
Total <%= roll.total %> against <%= roll.target %>.
<%= roll.grade_label %>, margin <%= margin %>.
<% if (clue = roll.clue_won) %>
This roll wins clue <%= clue %>.
<% end %>

<% if used.any? %>
Used since the scene began, already applied: <%= used.join(", ") %>.
<% end %>
<%= hero %> now: <%= character.sheet %>.
<% if (companions = scene.companions).any? %>
In the scene with <%= hero %>: <%= companions.map { it.character.portrait }.join("; ") %>.
<% end %>

<% if scene.last? %>
This is the last roll, and the story ends with it.
So far <%= attempts.join("; ") %>.
<% if (marks = game.marks).any? %>
What the rolls have changed so far: <%= marks.join(" / ") %>
All of it shows in the ending.
What was won is there to be used; what was lost and never won back is missing.
<% end %>
<% if (ending = roll.decided_ending) %>
A natural <%= roll.value %> decides the story alone: it ends in <%= ending %>.
<% else %>
Victory or defeat is the story's to decide: weigh what the heroes found and did against the plan's endings.
<% end %>
This roll decides whether their last move works.
A success gets them what they reached for; a failure gets them none of it, but undoes nothing won before.
Tell what this roll does, then the ending.
The ending rests on why it all happened, as the clues showed it; what the heroes never found stays unsaid.
The heroes settle the question with what they did<%= parts %>.
They make no move the players did not choose.
No one else steps in to win or lose it for them.
Tell it as scenes <%= witness %>, to the last line, not as a summary.
By the last line it is plain what became of each thing at stake and of the people it touched.
No one says what the story meant.
The block adds <%= ending ? %("outcome": "#{ending}") : %("outcome": "victory" or "defeat") %>.
<% elsif roll.life_at_stake? %>
This roll can take the last of <%= hero %>'s health.
<% if roll.last_hero_standing? %>
If it does, <%= hero %> falls and the story ends here in defeat: tell how, and add "outcome": "defeat" to the block.
If not, tell what this roll does and stop there.
<% else %>
If it does, <%= hero %> falls and takes no more turns, and the story goes on with the others: tell how.
Either way, tell what this roll does and stop there; the block has no outcome.
<% end %>
<% else %>
Tell what this roll does and stop there.
<% end %>
